CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constructed stream is good: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
no body for callee
--
N5008 [ostringstream.cons]/1, [basic.ios.cons] Table 128: a newly
constructed ostringstream has state goodbit.  The front end converts libc++'s
basic_ostringstream without drops (cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/
test_sstream.desc), but ios_base::init, ios_base::~ios_base and locale's
constructor and destructor are defined in libc++.so and had no models ("no
body for callee", bin53), so the stream state was nondeterministic.
provide_stdlib_bodies now models them by their specified effects, and
ios_base::clear ([iostate.flags]/4) and ios_base::getloc
([ios.base.locales]/4); test_postconditions.desc checks the Table 128
postconditions and setstate.  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts these
programs, and they fail only their WRONG assertion.
